<h1>Request Logging Middleware</h1>

<p>
    Request Logging Middleware is used to log information about every incoming HTTP request.
    It helps developers monitor application activity, debug issues, track requests,
    and analyze user behavior.
</p>

<hr />

<h3>Step 1: Create RequestLoggingMiddleware.cs File</h3>

<p>
    Create a new file named <strong>RequestLoggingMiddleware.cs</strong> inside the
    <strong>Middlewares</strong> folder.
</p>

<pre>
<code>
namespace Dotnet_Tutorials.Middlewares
{
    public class RequestLoggingMiddleware
    {
        private readonly RequestDelegate _next;

        public RequestLoggingMiddleware(RequestDelegate next)
        {
            _next = next;
        }

        public async Task InvokeAsync(HttpContext context)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("----- Incoming Request -----");

            Console.WriteLine($"Request Method: {context.Request.Method}");

            Console.WriteLine($"Request Path: {context.Request.Path}");

            Console.WriteLine($"Request Time: {DateTime.Now}");

            await _next(context);

            Console.WriteLine("----- Request Completed -----");
        }
    }
}
</code>
</pre>

<hr />

<h3>Step 2: Register the Middleware</h3>

<p>
    Register the middleware inside <strong>Program.cs</strong>.
</p>

<pre>
<code>
app.UseMiddleware&lt;RequestLoggingMiddleware&gt;();
</code>
</pre>

<p>
    Add this line before:
</p>

<pre>
<code>
app.UseRouting();
</code>
</pre>

<hr />

<h3>How It Works</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Middleware intercepts every incoming HTTP request.</li>
    <li>It accesses request details using <strong>HttpContext</strong>.</li>
    <li>The HTTP request method is retrieved using <strong>context.Request.Method</strong>.</li>
    <li>The request URL path is retrieved using <strong>context.Request.Path</strong>.</li>
    <li>The current request time is logged using <strong>DateTime.Now</strong>.</li>
    <li>The request is forwarded to the next middleware using <strong>await _next(context)</strong>.</li>
    <li>After response completion, a completion message is logged.</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<h3>Output Example</h3>

<pre>
<code>
----- Incoming Request -----

Request Method: GET

Request Path: /Home/Index

Request Time: 5/21/2026 10:45:12 AM

----- Request Completed -----
</code>
</pre>


